nce of independently verifiable Goal runs. Do not implement the milestones in this conversation. Execution belongs to `cruise queue run` or an explicit Goal invocation.\\\\n+\\\\n+Inspect the repository before asking questions. Ask only material questions whose answers change the decomposition: product intent, hard constraints, compatibility obligations, required migrations, and what must never break. Resolve ordinary implementation details from repository evidence. Do not demand approval phrases, plan digests, or ceremonial checkpoints.\\\\n+\\\\n+Compile the result into goal-sized milestones. Every milestone must have a one-line falsifiable outcome, its own verification commands, explicit likely touchpoints, explicit non-goals, protected invariants, and only real dependencies. A milestone should be independently completable; split work that cannot be verified without an unrelated later phase. Use non-goals to stop later concerns from bleeding into the current milestone.\\\\n+\\\\n+State cross-milestone reconciliation obligations once in the queue body. Include backward and forward compatibility, migration reversibility, coexistence windows, and cleanup conditions when they matter. Every generated flight plan inherits this body, so write obligations as constraints that remain meaningful throughout the queue.\\\\n+\\\\n+Write the compiled plan to `.cruise/QUEUE.md` using the pinned version 1 schema: `milestones` with `id`, `status`, `outcome`, `verify`, `depends`, `touchpoints`, `non_g<truncated omitted_approx_tokens=\\\"676\\\" />```\\\\n+\\\\n+Compile a project once, review the Markdown queue, then run each milestone as a\\\\n+supervised Goal on the selected provider:\\\\n+\\\\n+```sh\\\\n+cruise build -C ~/src/app \\\\\\\"Add a compatible parser migration\\\\\\\"\\\\n+cruise queue status -C ~/src/app\\\\n+cruise --codex queue run -C ~/src/app\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+| Launcher command | Purpose |\\\\n+| --- | --- |\\\\n+| `cruise <build|quick|refine|goal|debug> <request>` | Start one intent-based skill session. |\\\\n+| `cruise queue status` | Show milestone statuses and dependencies. |\\\\n+| `cruise queue run` | Run ready milestones sequentially as supervised Goals. |\\\\n+| `cruise worker [--level 1-7] <task>` | Run one bounded provider-native worker. |\\\\n+| `cruise doctor` | Check the selected local host integration. |\\\\n@@\\\\n-Every terminal invocation replaces `.cruise/ORIGIN.md` with that invocation's\\\\n-exact request. Direct plugin invocations do not create an Origin note; Goal\\\\n-execution may still maintain its advisory flight plan.\\\\n+Every terminal skill invocation replaces `.cruise/ORIGIN.md` with that\\\\n+invocation's exact request. Queue commands preserve that original build note\\\\n+and touch only `.cruise/QUEUE.md` and `.cruise/FLIGHT.md`. Direct plugin\\\\n+invocations do not create an Origin note; Goal execution may still maintain its\\\\n+advisory flight plan.\\\\n*** Update File: <PLUGIN_ROOT>/scripts/cruise.mjs\\\\n@@\\\\n-Cruise records the exact request in .cruise/ORIGIN.md; Goal runs may also keep\\\\n-an advisory .cruise/FLIGHT.md. Codex Goal loops use evidence-based stall\\\\n-supervision and pause with a report after a realignment and final experiment.\\\\n+Cruise records exact skill requests in .cruise/ORIGIN.md. Build may compile an\\\\n+advisory .cruise/QUEUE.md; queue run turns each ready milestone into an advisory\\\\n+.cruise/FLIGHT.md and executes it as a supervised Goal, stopping on failure.\\\\n+Codex Goal loops pause with a report after realignment and a final experiment.\\\\n*** End Patch\\\";text(await tools.apply_patch(patch))\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"\\n[103] tool exec result: Script completed\\nWall time 0.8 seconds\\nOutput:\\n\\n{}\\n\"},{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"\\n[104] tool exec call: const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"npm test && node scripts/cruise.mjs --help && claude plugin validate . && git diff --check\\\",workdir:\\\"<PLUGIN