{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '35,120p' <PLUGIN_ROOT>/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"and keeps its status truthful. You may edit it at any time; it is advisory and\ngrants or gates nothing. The selected host's native permissions remain the only\nauthority for work and effects.\n\n## Build queues\n\nBuild inspects the repository, clarifies only material product and compatibility\nquestions, and writes goal-sized milestones to `.cruise/QUEUE.md`. Each\nmilestone owns an outcome, verification, dependency list, touchpoints,\nnon-goals, and invariants. Cross-milestone compatibility obligations live once\nin the Markdown body and are inherited by every generated flight plan.\n\nThe queue is user-editable and advisory. Reorder or adjust it between milestone\nruns, then inspect or execute it with `cruise queue status` and\n`cruise queue run`. Queue execution is sequential: it never skips a blocked or\nstalled milestone, and it stops with a report instead of inventing authority.\n\n## Provider integration\n\nCruise shares its skills and terminal UI, but not its host control plane:\n\n| Surface | Codex | Claude Code |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Skill syntax | `$cruise:goal` | `/cruise:goal` |\n| Plugin manifest | `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` | `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` |\n| Task transport | Codex app-server | Native interactive `claude` process |\n| Planning | Native Plan collaboration mode | Native `/plan` or `--permission-mode plan` when planning-only is requested |\n| Autonomous goal | Native Goal lifecycle and status | In-session task list and execution loop; no documented equivalent Goal lifecycle API is exposed to plugins |\n| Pause/resume | Native Goal pause plus task continuation | `Ctrl-C`, `/resume`, `--continue`, and `--resume` |\n| Workers | Live Codex model catalog and reasoning effort | Claude model aliases and native effort levels |\n\nThe terminal launcher defaults to Codex, preserving the existing behavior.\nSelect Claude for one invocation with `--claude`, or select Codex explicitly\nwith `--codex`. `--provider codex|claude` and the request-scoped\n`CRUISE_PROVIDER` environment variable are equivalent. Conflicting selectors\nare rejected.\n\n## Install\n\nThe plugins require a signed-in Codex or Claude Code installation. The optional\nterminal launcher also requires Node.js 20 or later.\n\n### Codex plugin\n\nInstall Cruise from a configured Codex plugin marketplace, then start a new\ntask:\n\n```sh\ncodex plugin marketplace list\ncodex plugin add cruise@<marketplace-name>\ncodex plugin list\n```\n\nFor example, the local development marketplace is commonly named\n`agent-local`.\n\n### Claude Code plugin\n\nValidate and load a local checkout directly:\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin validate .\nclaude --plugin-dir .\n```\n\nFor a distributed install, add the marketplace that contains Cruise and install\nits namespaced entry:\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin marketplace add <marketplace-source>\nclaude plugin install cruise@<marketplace-name>\nclaude plugin list\n```\n\n### Terminal launcher (optional)\n\n```sh\nnpm install --global cruise-code\ncruise --help\n```\n\nFrom a checkout, use `node scripts/cruise.mjs --help` or run `npm link` once.\n\n## Use Cruise\n\nInvoke the same lane with the host's native command character:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' <PLUGIN_ROOT>/scripts/lib/flight-plan.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"import { lstat, mkdir, readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\n\nexport const FLIGHT_FILE = '.cruise/FLIGHT.md';\nexport const DEFAULT_STALL = Object.freeze({ quietTurns: 3, sameFailure: 3 });\n\nconst STATUSES = new Set(['active', 'complete', 'blocked']);\nconst KNOWN_KEYS = new Set(['version', 'status', 'outcome', 'verify', 'scope', 'invariants', 'stall']);\n\nfunction isObject(value) {\n  return value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction stripComment(value) {\n  let quote = null;\n  let escaped = false;\n  for (let index = 0; index < value.length; index += 1) {\n    const character = value[index];\n    if (quote === '\"' && character === '\\\\' && !escaped) {\n      escaped = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (character === quote && !escaped) quote = null;\n    else if (!quote && (character === '\"' || character === \"'\")) quote = character;\n    else if (!quote && character === '#' && (index === 0 || /\\s/u.test(value[index - 1]))) {\n      return value.slice(0, index).trimEnd();\n    }\n    escaped = false;\n  }\n  if (quote) throw new Error('unterminated quoted scalar');\n  return value.trimEnd();\n}\n\nfunction parseScalar(value) {\n  const scalar = value.trim();\n  if (scalar === '[]') return [];\n  if (scalar === '{}') return {};\n  if (scalar === 'null' || scalar === '~') return null;\n  if (scalar === 'true') return true;\n  if (scalar === 'false') return false;\n  if (/^-?(?:0|[1-9]\\d*)(?:\\.\\d+)?$/u.test(scalar)) return Number(scalar);\n  if (scalar.startsWith('\"')) {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(scalar);\n    if (typeof parsed !== 'string') throw new Error('quoted values must be strings');\n    return parsed;\n  }\n  if (scalar.startsWith(\"'\")) {\n    if (!scalar.endsWith(\"'\"